From 808e303565883f3eba9fa2a8199ea05b45e09e76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deadband Session <assistant@deadband.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:49:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Two-squad hierarchy: squad_hall scene, authority reads
 the squads block

- scenes/squad_hall.yaml: 30x20 hall, gcs + six cars in two squads (alpha:
  car1 leads car2,car3; bravo: car4 leads car5,car6). Exists because hierarchy
  is only structurally distinct from a star at two or more squads. NOT a model
  of the real lab - lab_box keeps the three cars that actually exist.
- missions/squad_patrol.yaml: tasking so the hierarchy has something to command.
- lab_box on the new schema (authority/routing/squads) with ONE squad, which is
  what three cars honestly support.
- fix: command_authority() never read the squads block, so every agent reported
  straight to the coordinator - a hierarchy in routing but not in authority.
  Now resolves members->leader, leader->coordinator.
- command_authority() reads the new 'authority' key (architecture/topology kept
  as legacy aliases).

First real result, blast radius over squad_hall (agents losing authority when
one node is removed):
    centralized    worst 6/6, mean 0.86
    hierarchical   worst 2/6, mean 0.29
    decentralized  worst 0/6, mean 0.00
Hierarchy bounds the damage to the tier that lost its decider. Removing a
squad leader costs nothing because members fall back to the coordinator -
graceful degradation, worth stating explicitly rather than leaving implicit.
